Z||000000||ChadMan||04-16-2000||09:33 AM||||So there I was, coming home from a visit to 87ECO5's place yesterday afternoon.  Light traffic, sunny day, dry roads, great visibility.  I crest a hill, and who's waiting for me but John Law.  In a red Fiero, I'm dead meat.<P>Not only does he write me for 81 in a 65, but he checks the "Unsafe for Conditions" box.  Give me a GD break...if this clown really thought driving 81 in perfect conditions was unsafe, he wouldn't have a job that required him to drive 100+ mph!<P>I've been lucky - it's been five years since I had to pay the "go-fast tax."  Still, it's a pi$$er.<P>Thanks for letting me rant.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Eric||04-16-2000||10:24 AM||||So where was this Fiero hater stationed?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-16-2000||10:26 AM||||Sorry about the ticket.  The dangers of having a nice riding car.  I've gotten a few in the past, but a long time ago.  The last one was for 50 in a 35 zone in a 72 Vega GT wagon.  That car couldn't hit 80 mph falling off a cliff. The Vega was rated the second most worst car ever made, only the Yugo beat it out.<P>Not that I still don't go over the limit, I haven't been caught.  Lucky me. ||||reg||9
