Z||000005||stimpy||04-16-2000||11:16 AM||||Grrr! I found out the price on my ticket for failure to use turn signal, - $70!! Open container of beer would only have been $50. Can we say screwed up priorities? Of course, with the police department having already eradicated real crime in our fair city, they are worth every dime. Just the price to pay to live in a city that has no murders, rapists or child molesters!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||04-16-2000||05:44 PM||||ya...the only prob wiht having a nice little sports car that catches the eye...is it also catches those cops too..<P>ever since i got my fiero ive had cops u-turn on the highway and follow me for a while, i get dirty looks whenever i pass a cop now.....and iin my small town the fiero must be in the cops "list" or something...cause whenever i see  one in town..sure enough he follows me for a while..||||reg||1
Z||000007||Patrick||04-16-2000||08:30 PM||||<BR>Hmmm... a week or so ago I would have thought that maybe some of you guys were getting a little paranoid about cops and Fieros. However, a few days ago I got pulled over by a motorcycle cop while I was driving my Fiero. I knew beyond a shadow of a doubt that I had done nothing illegal. (Not this time anyway <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) He asked me for my license which I gave to him. Then he asked me if it was my car. I said yes. He asked me a second time! I said yes a second time. He then said I had done nothing wrong, that it was just a <I>routine check</I>. He handed my license back and walked away. It was odd that he never asked to see my registration papers. I don't know what this <I>routine check</I> nonsense was all about, but I wasn't going to bother pursuing it...<P>------------------------------------------------------------------------<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick (edited 04-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierospeeder||04-16-2000||11:56 PM||||I just got a speeding ticket on Friday.  Going to my friends house and im 3 blocks away from my house.  Im driving my tbird turbo.  I turned onto the street sped up, no idea how fast i was going then i hit my brakes because there was cars in front of me, i take a turn left and was driving on the busy street.  After a few seconds i see lights flashing, i pull over and says i got you going 50 in a 35.    He also complained i had no front license plate, i told him i dont have a plate holder, if you notice on a tbird turbo 87 it is a 45 degree angle in the nose.  And im missing the holder, so he hassled about that to me.  I have to pay 95 including school fees for my ticket.  Otherwise 75 but it would be in my records.  Its been more then a year, and it blows.  I probably only hit 50 for a few seconds and got caught in traffic.  <P>I guess i have to hold off on buying a new stator for my motorcycle now, bought the bike from my friend.  <BR>Wheres the kewl cops that give 30 dollar warnings.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ChadMan||04-17-2000||08:28 AM||||Eric, Officer Bagadonuts was stationed on I-270 just north of Roberts Rd.<P>Fiero64, thanks for the tip, but I'm going to be in AZ on my court date and don't want to hassle with a continuance.  Otherwise I probably would make up some cockamamie story and go to court - if the officer doesn't show, you win your case.<P>87ECO5, don't feel bad - I probably would have been driving that fast even if I weren't in a hurry!  I was just glad to meet your wife and hang out with you, Drew and WTIII.  Angie thought it was funny and called me "Mario."<P>Stimpy, if you didn't cause a wreck or nearly cause one by not signaling, the cop that wrote you is a serious a$$hole IMHO.  Of course it's important to signal, but I see so many cops ignore this every day - why single you out?<P>Thanks for everybody's responses.  Misery loves company!||||reg||1
