Z||000019||bHooper||04-17-2000||03:57 PM||||a few years back, i was driving home (about 10:30 at nite) when a car dangerously pulled out in front of me (i was doing the speed limit 55mph), causing me to have to severely brake and slow down.  it was obvious that this guy cut me off.  but the next thing i know, there are blue lights behind me!  i got pulled over!<P>i asked the "cop" whats the problem, and <B>told</B> him that i new for certain that i had done nothing wrong.  he asked for my license, then said "i didnt think you had your seat belt on".  <P>i told him, it was very obvious that i did and he should not be bothering me when the car in front created a dangerouse situation!  then he asked for me to get out of the car and started checking me for alcohol!  <P>it was at this point i realized that he was a airport security officer and had <B>NO</B> authority whatsoever... so i told him what i thought of his harassment, got back in my GT and went home!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>shouldnt pick on us Fiero people... we are probably smarter than you think!||||reg||1
Z||000020||Cliff Pennock||04-17-2000||08:23 PM||||Yeah, I once told an airport security officer what I thought of him. I still shrug at the sight of rubber gloves...||||reg||11
Z||000021||stimpy||04-17-2000||08:31 PM||||Yeah Chad, you are right about Officer A. Neil Orifice. Punk was about 15 years old- Doogie Howser P.D.  One of the reaons why I didn't signal is I was too busy checking over my shoulder to see that the lane was clear. Not a car to be seen. <BR>Fighting the ticket would require missing a couple of days from work and wearing thin the good favor of my boss however. Then there is always the chance one of our Law and Order Bible belt judges would find me guilty and I'd wind up far worse then paying the pinche $70 fine.  ||||reg||1
